      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Henri for the suggestion, agreed it reads better. I applied the syntax change to avctp.pdl, but regenerating avctp.py with the in-tree pdlc (v0.3.3, from out/soong/.../pdlc) produced two issues I wanted to flag.\n\nFirst, the bit shifts on the parent AvctpPacket come out LSB-first even though the file declares big_endian_packets. For example transaction_label ends up at byte0 \u0026 0xf instead of byte0 \u003e\u003e 4, which would misparse every AVCTP header.\n\nSecond, AvctpContinuePacket is dropped from the try-chain in AvctpPacket.parse. Only AvctpSinglePacket and AvctpStartPacket are tried; CONTINUE and END both fall through to the bare base class.\n\nAre these known limitations of this pdlc version, or should I be running a different one? Happy to land just the .pdl change and keep the existing .py for now if that works.",
